---
title: CLI
description: CarvePress command-line commands and flags generated from the implemented CLI behavior.
order: 1
---

# CLI

Run CarvePress with `carve-press <command> [options]`. If the first argument is an option, `build` is assumed.

## Commands

| Command | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `build` | Build the site. |
| `check` | Run every build check without writing a build. |
| `fmt [paths...]` | Format `.crv` sources in place, `srcDir` by default. |
| `import <source>` | Convert Markdown or HTML pages into `.crv` pages. |
| `routes` | Print discovered routes and source files. |
| `dev` | Build, serve, watch, and live reload. |
| `serve` | Serve the existing `outDir`. |
| `init` | Scaffold a new site. |
| `new <path>` | Create a new page under `srcDir`. |
| `help` | Print help. |

## Flags

| Flag | Applies To | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `--root <dir>` | all commands | current working directory | Project root. |
| `--port <n>` | `dev`, `serve` | `5173` for dev, `4173` for serve | Server port from `0` through `65535`; invalid values fall back. |
| `--host <host>` | `dev`, `serve` | `127.0.0.1` | Server host. |
| `--open` | `dev` | off | Open the dev server URL in a browser. |
| `--force` | `init`, `import` | off | Allow existing files to be overwritten. |
| `--title <title>` | `new` | title-cased file name | Page title for a new page. |
| `--check` | `fmt` | off | List files that would change and exit 1 instead of writing them. |
| `--align-tables` | `fmt` | off | Pad table columns to a shared display width. |
| `--out <dir>` | `import` | `srcDir`, or `docs` without a config | Directory the pages are written to. |
| `--from <format>` | `import` | by file extension | Convert only `markdown` or `html`. Required for a single file whose extension is neither. |
| `--report <file>` | `import` | off | Write the full report, every finding included, as JSON. |
| `--help` | all commands | off | Print help. |
| `--version` | all commands | off | Print the package version. |

## Checking a Site

`check` renders every page, lints it and its includes, and validates links, nav, sidebars, prev/next overrides and the route manifest, exactly as `build` does. The output goes to a temporary directory that is removed afterwards, so `outDir` and `routes.json` are left untouched. Any failure exits with a non-zero status, which makes it a pull-request gate:

```bash "CI step"
npx carve-press check
```

## Formatting Sources

`fmt` rewrites `.crv` files with the Carve engine's canonical writer. With no paths it formats every `.crv` under `srcDir`, including snippets that `srcExclude` keeps out of routing; hidden directories and `node_modules` are skipped. Pass files or directories to format only those.

`--check` writes nothing: it prints each file that is not canonical and exits 1 if there is any. `--align-tables` pads every table column to a common width, measured by display width. It is opt-in, so use the same flag in `--check` and in the formatting run, or the two disagree.

A file the writer cannot format is reported with the reason and the command exits 2.

## Importing a Site

`import` moves an existing Markdown or HTML site to Carve. Point it at a file or a directory:

```bash "migrate a VitePress docs folder"
carve-press import old-docs --report import-report.json
```

Each `.md`, `.markdown`, `.html` or `.htm` file becomes a `.crv` page at the same relative path under `--out`, which defaults to the configured `srcDir`. Other files, such as images next to the pages, are copied alongside so relative references keep working. Hidden directories (`.vitepress`, `.git`) and `node_modules` are skipped, and an existing file in the target is never overwritten unless `--force` is given.

Markdown goes through the engine's Markdown importer, which keeps YAML frontmatter. For HTML, the first `<main>`, else `<article>`, else `<body>` is taken as the page content, so site navigation and footers stay behind; a page without an H1 gets its `<title>` as the frontmatter title.

The terminal report lists every finding that lost or degraded content, with its file and line: elements the HTML importer dropped, Markdown constructs it could only approximate, and links that still name a source file such as `../index.md`. CarvePress routes have no extension, so those links need pointing at the route. The `--report` file carries every finding, informational ones too. After an import, run `carve-press check` to see what the build would still reject.

## Examples

```bash "common commands"
carve-press build
carve-press check
carve-press fmt --check --align-tables
carve-press fmt docs/guide --align-tables
carve-press import old-docs --out docs --report import-report.json
carve-press routes --root .
carve-press dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173
carve-press serve --port 4173
carve-press init --force
carve-press new guide/install --title "Install"
```

Unknown commands print usage and exit with a non-zero status. User-facing build errors are formatted without raw stack traces.

